faster-enhancer.c
====

faster-enhancer.c is a native C/SIMD inference engine derived from the FastEnhancer-Medium
model architecture and pretrained ONNX release.

FastEnhancer
------------

Original project:
  FastEnhancer: Speed-Optimized Streaming Neural Speech Enhancement
  https://github.com/aask1357/fastenhancer

Original author and license:
  Copyright (c) 2025 AHN Sung Hwan
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The bundled `weights/fe.q8` blob is a quantized derivative of the
FastEnhancer-Medium pretrained model. The original copyright notice and MIT
license terms are preserved here for the model-derived components.

Third-party techniques
----------------------

No third-party source code is included in this repository. The following
projects informed the design of the int8 GEMM micro-kernels; the algorithmic
patterns were reimplemented, not copied. Their licenses are listed for
attribution only.

  ggml / llama.cpp   MIT          NEON i16-level vmull/vmlal/vpadalq fusion
  XNNPACK            BSD-3-Clause AVX2 vpmovsxbw + vpmaddwd saturation-free dot
  oneDNN             Apache-2.0   x86 int8 GEMM blocking conventions
  ARM KleidiAI       Apache-2.0   I8MM A row-pair pre-pack layout

See the Sources table in docs/optimizations.md for the specific references.

